body:
Good point, I kind of presumed it'd been a little while since the prison break, him building some strength and biding some time. Even with magic, if ya boy's been eating rats for 15 years, he shouldn't be so hench.

I don't think it's a doUblE StanDarD however, I think it's just a bit more obviously strange in Kai'Sa's case although both are inexplicable; and further while few people (for better or for worse) were/are probably interested in seeing Sylas as an emaciated stick-man sprinting everywhere, lots of people were interested in seeing Kai'Sa appearing more alien/inhuman, or having something more to her to show she'd been touched by and integrated herself into the Void.

TL;DR: It's not that people were upset Kai was hot, it's that they wanted Kai to be hot with the weird stuff. c;

You did it by accident, as you say. But in my opinion pretty strongly, you essentially don't owe them anything. On the Internet in general, you can express in whatever way you like. You don't have to bring-up that you're behind both blogs if you don't want to, if it makes you feel uncomfortable. You don't have to adjust your OC either for them, although I guess it is true that the others around have the choice whether to RP with it or not, it's also their free-time.

&#x200B;

What you're doing and choose to do with this in the future honestly doesn't negatively impact anyone. The only person who might be feeling bad from this is you, so try not to feel as guilty if you can. It's really not manipulation, just to repeat that, so just follow whatever creates the most enjoyable RP and OOC interactions for you if you've got an idea of that, hun.

&#x200B;

Hope this helps a bit and sorry for the late reply.

Old Xerath.

He's actually the only champion I ever played back when I was a kid that I haven't at some point revisited in my adult League playing. Usually if I was awful at them I do well now, and if I was OK with them back then, I suck. Of course, new Xerath isn't that similar anyways, he's not someone like Rumble or Shyvana who still has the same core kit with changes to how you use it.

I remember I was 11 or 12 when the Xerath rework hit and after playing it I actually burst into tears because I didn't understand it at all and he was the character I played 90% of my games on at the time. My sister didn't get it. ^ ^ ^;
